## Story Description
The test backend/tests/test_ingestion_api.py::TestStatus::test_get_status_known_job_returns_row fails with KeyError: 'batch_id'. The get_job_status router in backend/app/routers/ingestion.py (around line 138) reads row['batch_id'] from the SQL SELECT result. The _MOCK_JOB dict in the test file (around line 30) was written before batch_id was added to the pipeline_jobs table in the Data Model Hardening sprint. The fix is to add 'batch_id': None to _MOCK_JOB so the mock mapping returns None for that key.

## Acceptance Criteria
- Edit file: backend/tests/test_ingestion_api.py — add key-value pair 'batch_id': None to the _MOCK_JOB dict
- Run: python3 -m pytest backend/tests/test_ingestion_api.py::TestStatus::test_get_status_known_job_returns_row -v — must show PASSED
- Run: python3 -m pytest backend/tests/ -v 2>&1 | tail -5 — must show 0 failed

